## What This Chart Installs

- A DaemonSet running [node-problem-detector](https://github.com/kubernetes/node-problem-detector)
  on every Linux node, tolerating all taints. It reads `/dev/kmsg` with the monitor configs baked
  into the image, so they always match the binary:

  | Monitor | Node conditions |
  |---------|-----------------|
  | `kernel-monitor` | `KernelDeadlock`, `XfsShutdown`, `CperHardwareErrorFatal` |
  | `readonly-monitor` | `ReadonlyFilesystem` |

  Both monitors also emit kernel problems as events.
- A ServiceAccount and a ClusterRoleBinding to the built-in `system:node-problem-detector`
  ClusterRole, which kube-apiserver creates as part of its bootstrap RBAC policy.

Nothing is configurable: the chart's only consumers are NKS platform releases, which pin a chart
version immutably, so any change is a new chart release.

## Upgrading node-problem-detector

Bump `appVersion` in [Chart.yaml](Chart.yaml) in a `fix(deps):` or `feat:` commit. Release-please
then opens the chart release PR.

